contentText:
From the football field to the dance floor, Rob Gronkowski is excited to party it up at Taylor Swift and Travis Kelce&#8217;s wedding.

In an interview with Page Six , the retired NFL tight end spoke about his upcoming annual music festival Gronk Beach and whether or not Kelce will be in attendance. &#8220;Travis Kelce is always invited to Gronk Beach,&#8221; Gronkowski said. &#8220;We hit it off. It&#8217;s where we first kind of officially met.&#8221;

He explains that he and Kelce met at the festival in Vegas in 2022 when the Chainsmokers took the stage. He also shares that, in a full-circle moment, he, Kelce and the EDM duo reunited this year at a Sports Illustrated party. As a result of how much fun they had together, Kelce has secured himself an annual invite to Gronk Beach.

In return, Page Six inquired if Gronk was invited to the upcoming Tayvis wedding. &#8220;Oh my gosh, my lips are sealed,&#8221; Gronk replied. &#8220;I may or may not be invited to the wedding.&#8221;

While we don&#8217;t know if Gronk will be there, we do know what kind of wedding guest he plans to be.

&#8220;If I am, I can tell you this: I&#8217;m going to be bringing Gronk Beach energy to it,&#8221; he told Page Six . &#8220;He may want to invite me because I bring the juice to the table — to the dance floor.&#8221;

Though the former football star did not officially reveal if he will be in attendance, we know that it&#8217;s quite likely he could be invited. In an October 2025 appearance on The Graham Norton Show , Swift shared that the guest list for her upcoming nuptials will be extensive.

&#8220;I know it’s going to be fun to plan because I think the only stressful weddings are the ones where you have a small amount, and people are on the bubble,&#8221; Swift says of putting together the invite list. &#8220;And you have to evaluate or assess your relationship with them to see if they should be there. I’m not going to do that.&#8221;

Swift joked with Norton that the party will be filled with &#8220;anyone [she&#8217;s] ever talked to.&#8221;
